[*
*   rdn file that will be loaded at the runtime
*   term.rdn is hight level layer of Terminal manipulations
*   it protect backward complatible in case the native layer API has been 
*   upgraded or changed
* *]

[*
*  rmp_to_raw_mode: function that accept boolean 
*  true to raw mode false not
*  and returns boolean indicate the error
*  example:
*       (true) rmp_to_raw_mode call -> boolean
* *]
rmp_to_raw_mode defun
    tha-list let

    tha-list type "list" != if
        false
    else
        tha-list 0 index [* boolean *]
        rmp_to_raw_mode_native call
    end
end

[*
*   rmp_get_term_size: function that push two values into the stack
*   as return value width and height of the function
*   otherwise it push two null value indicates that is error
*   example:
*       rmp_get_term_size call -> integer? integer?
* *]
rmp_get_term_size defun
    rmp_get_term_size call
end

[*
*   rmp_init_terminal: always intial terminal first
* *]
rmp_init_terminal defun
    rmp_init_terminal_native call
end

[*
*   rmp_restore_terminal: and don't forget to restore the og one
* *]
rmp_restore_terminal defun
    rmp_restore_terminal call
end
